+ # Brest-Litovsk & Soviet Diplomacy Events
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.1.t:0 "Soviet Peace Overtures at Brest-Litovsk"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.1.d:0 "The newly formed Bolshevik Council of People's Commissars has proclaimed the Decree on Peace, appealing for an immediate cessation of hostilities. Envoys under Adolf Joffe have arrived at the German headquarters in Brest-Litovsk seeking an armistice. Field Marshal von Hindenburg and General Ludendorff present our stark choice: dictate severe territorial terms stripping Russia of its western provinces, or resume the offensive eastward."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.1.a:0 "Dictate our terms! Cede the borderlands or face destruction!"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.1.b:0 "Refuse negotiations! The German army will march to Petrograd!"
+ GER_dictate_brest_litovsk_tt:0 "Present an ultimatum demanding the independence and cession of Poland, Lithuania, and Ukraine."
+ GER_refuse_peace_talks_tt:0 "Hostilities continue unabated across the Eastern Front."
+
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.2.t:0 "The German Ultimatum: The Treaty of Brest-Litovsk"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.2.d:0 "At Brest-Litovsk, the German delegation headed by General Max Hoffmann has laid down an iron ultimatum. Russia must surrender sovereignty over Poland, Lithuania, Courland, and recognize Ukrainian and Finnish independence. The Bolshevik leadership is bitterly fractured: Lenin urges accepting the 'shameful peace' to preserve Soviet power, Bukharin demands revolutionary war, and Trotsky champions 'neither war nor peace'."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.2.a:0 "Sign the Treaty. The Soviet Republic needs breathing space!"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.2.b:0 "Neither war nor peace! Trotsky walks out of negotiations!"
+ SOV_brest_litovsk_signed_tt:0 "Conclude an immediate white peace with the Central Powers. Germany secures grain and raw material deliveries."
+ SOV_trotsky_walkout_tt:0 "Trotsky denounces imperialist annexations and walks out, leaving the front wide open to German advance."
+
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.3.t:0 "Operation Faustschlag: The German Spring Offensive"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.3.d:0 "Following the Soviet delegation's refusal to sign the treaty, Supreme Army Command has launched Operation Faustschlagâ€”the 'Fist Punch'. With the old Russian army completely disintegrated and Red Guards offering token resistance, fifty German divisions advance eastward along railway lines at lightning speed, overrunning Dvinsk, Minsk, and Kiev."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.3.a:0 "Forward across the rails! Nothing can halt our advance!"
+
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.4.t:0 "The Front Collapses: Faustschlag Overruns the East"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.4.d:0 "The German advance is unstoppable. German columns are rolling across Ukraine, Belarus, and Estonia aboard armored trains. With German vanguards mere days from Petrograd, Lenin's faction demands an emergency vote: accept even more humiliating terms now, or perish under the German jackboot."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.4.a:0 "Sign the peace at once! We have no army left to fight!"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.4.b:0 "Fight to the last proletarian! No surrender to the Kaiser!"
+ SOV_faustschlag_capitulation_tt:0 "Capitulate to the German demands under fire. Exits the war with the Central Powers."
+
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.20.t:0 "The Collapse of Brest-Litovsk"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.20.d:0 "With the collapse and armistice of the German Empire in the West, the draconian Treaty of Brest-Litovsk is officially voided! Soviet authorities in Moscow have declared the treaty null and void, as German garrisons withdraw from Ukraine, Belarus, and the Baltic. A vast power vacuum opens across Eastern Europe, beckoning the Red Army westward."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.20.a:0 "The imperialist treaty is torn to shreds! Westward ho!"
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.20.b:0 "Our eastern dominion crumbles into dust..."
+ ww1_russia_diplomacy.20.c:0 "The German hegemony in the East has evaporated."
+ SOV_target_vistula_reclamation_tt:0 "The Treaty of Brest-Litovsk is dissolved! Soviet westward reclamation begins."
+
